{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1550321-trying-to-explain-every-curseborne-family-as-quickly-as-possible","id":1550321,"title":"Trying to Explain Every Curseborne Family as Quickly as possible","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-04-22T13:10:01-07:00","id":1550321,"title":"Trying to Explain Every Curseborne Family as Quickly as possible","content":"Trying to Explain Every Curseborne Family as Quickly as possible. With as little &quot;Its like X from Y&quot;:<ul><li><b>Furies</b> - Vengeful ghosts.</li> <li><b>Mavens </b>- Adrenaline junky ghosts.</li> <li><b>Poltergeists</b> - Ghosts that haunt places and people.</li> <li><b>Shades </b>- Tormenting ghosts.</li> <li><b>Wardens</b> - Overly protective, guardian ghosts.</li> <li><b>Zeds</b> - Corporate assassin ghosts.</li> <li><b>Ascetics</b> - Memory/knowledge vampires that act as information brokers.</li> <li><b>The Black Hearts</b> - Emotional vampires that act as mercenaries.</li> <li><b>Gaki</b>- Ghost eating vampires that act like necromancers.</li> <li><b>Heirs</b>- Old money vampires that run corporations and eat hearts.</li> <li><b>House Bathory</b> - New money vampires that pretend to be royalty and bathe in blood.</li> <li><b>Iscariots </b>- Flesh eating vampires that believe betrayal is for the greater good.</li> <li><b>Vorare </b>- Soul eating vampires that are akin to demons.</li> <li><b>The Battleground Angels</b> - Zealot soldiers that like to fight the Outsiders.</li> <li><b>The Chimerae</b> - Mutated people who got too close to godhood and were cursed.</li> <li><b>The Nephilim</b> - Information broker demons.</li> <li><b>Keepers of the Broken Vine</b> - Creatures that build paradises.</li> <li><b>Munificents</b> - Wish granting genies.</li> <li><b>League of the Hidden Crossroads </b>- Deal with the devil types.</li> <li><b>The Eight Hands </b>- Werespiders/insects that create webs of connections between people.</li> <li><b>Get of Lyka</b> - Werewolves/canines that are territorial and combative.</li> <li><b>The Hydes</b> - Dr. Jekyll/Mr Hyde transformers that are scientifically minded.</li> <li><b>The Raptors</b> - Were-feathered reptiles that have the most knowledge of Curses.</li> <li><b>Spawn of Vodnik</b> - Were-fish/aquatic creatures that hoard treasure.</li> <li><b>The Sphinx </b>- Werecats/felines that said to guard the dead and hoard treasure.</li> <li><b>Archivists </b>- Sacrifice knowledge to cast spells. Information broker types.</li> <li><b>The Faceless</b> - Sacrifice noteriety and spoils of crimes to cast spells. Criminals for hire.</li> <li><b>The Network</b> - Sacrifice relationships to cast spells. Build relationships with others until they are ready to burn them, like a pyramid scheme.</li> <li><b>The Premiere </b>- Sacrifice time/obligations to cast spells. Oldest unbroken line of sorcerers about heritage and pedigree.</li> <li><b>Reeves</b> - Sacrifice life and death to cast spells. See themselves as gardeners of their life and prune away the weeds</li> <li><b>The Unburdened</b> - Sacrifice material possessions to cast spells. Akin to a socialist commune.</li> </ul>What do you think? Anything too off base?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-22T16:28:01-07:00","id":1550324,"title":"","content":"Mostly pretty good. From the lore videos, slight revisions:<br /> <br /> Heirs: Old money vampires that eat hearts and recognize the value of good minions.<br /> <br /> House Bathory: New money vampires that pretend to be warrior royalty and bathe in blood.<br /> <br /> Vorare: Soul eating vampires who think of themselves as dark, demon-powered superheroes.<br /> <br /> Chimerae: Mutated people who got too close to godhood and were cursed, and saw that as no reason to stop.<br /> <br /> Munificents: Tricksters who destroy the foolish and greedy by granting their wishes a la Monkey's Paw.<br /> <br /> League of the Hidden Crossroads: Honorable deal with the devil types who work like the mafia.<br /> <br /> Hydes: Dr. Jekyll/Mr Hyde transformers that are scientifically minded and use their alternate forms as tools, especially welding torches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-23T16:03:09-07:00","id":1550350,"title":"","content":"This is an amazing thread. I would be either a Black Heart, a Nephilim or a Sphinx if I were playing Curseborne.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 04-23-2025, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key